<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Upi</h1><p class="st-meta">1500 BCE – 1200 BCE (approx.) · capital Damascus</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Upi, the Late Bronze Age territory of Damascus, the southernmost Syrian land held by Egypt and a frontier with the Hittites.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Upi, or Apa, was the oasis of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> and the land around it. It came under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/egyptian-empire-new-kingdom">Egyptian Empire New Kingdom</a> after the campaigns of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thutmose-iii">Thutmose III</a> in the 15th century BCE, forming one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt's</a> provinces in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syrian-arab-republic">Syria</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amarna-letters">Amarna letters</a>, the local ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/biryawaza">Biryawaza</a> acted as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt's</a> agent, defending the area against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-empire">Hittites</a> and their allies such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aitakkama">Aitakkama</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kadesh">Kadesh</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> served as a base for Egyptian officials and troops.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Upi remained the Egyptian border district after the Battle of Kadesh and the peace treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramesses-ii">Ramesses II</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hattusili-iii">Hattusili III</a> c. 1259 BCE. With the collapse of Egyptian power after 1200 BCE, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> later rose again as the capital of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/aram-damascus">Aram-Damascus</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1500 BCE – 1200 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:29.85%;width:5.97%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1500 BCE – 1200 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century-bce">16th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century-bce">13th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Damascus</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Biryawaza</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Syrian Semitic religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Akkadian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/syria">Syria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Apa, Canaanite Damascus</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-1350&amp;focus=upi" aria-label="Upi on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5607 962 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Upi lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5927 1218L5863 1489"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5863 1489h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5927 1218h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5927 1218h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Damascus. <a href="/atlas?year=-1350&amp;focus=upi">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

